NewAircad is open to everyoneDraft, model, and document. Together.Precision 2D drafting and 3D modeling, with multiplayer editing and an AI agent that drafts, models, and renders alongside you.Start for FreeSee what's insideRead the docsWoven Grove Pavilion - Aircadaircad.com/f/woven-grove-pavilion9:41No installsOpen a browser and start drawing, always on the latest version.Pro 2D & 3D draftingPrecision drafting and solid modeling in one app.Version historyEvery change is on record.Opens your DWGsWith their layouts, blocks, and dimensions.01/Drafting & 3DPro 2D & pro 3D in one app.2D drafting and 3D solid modeling in one fast, beautiful workspace, from a command line that takes the shortcuts you already know.Browse every commandCopperlight Library - Aircadaircad.com/f/copperlight-libraryFamiliar drafting toolsTrim, split, extend, stretch, arcs, hatches, blocks, and layers, with command line precision and snaps.NURBS-based solid modelingBooleans, fillets, shells, lofts, and sweeps.Push/pull modelingPick a face and push or pull it with precision.Block libraries built inDoors, windows, furniture, and plumbing in Imperial and Metric, plus your team’s own blocks, shared in one place.02/AIPowerful AI on your terms.Ask a question or describe an edit in plain words, and the agent works right in your drawing.How the agent worksDoes this stair meet code?Checking the stair against the IRCFloor to floor is 9′-4″ (112″) over 14 risers: 8″ each, over the 7¾″ limit. Treads are 11″ (10″ minimum). 112 ÷ 7.75 = 14.45, so 15 risers at 7.47″. With the top landing fixed, the new tread goes at the bottom, so check the bottom landing (36″ minimum) and headroom (6′-8″ minimum).Read the file overviewRead the fileOpen in ScriptsNo. Its 14 risers are 8″ each (9′-4″ floor to floor), and the IRC allows 7¾″. The 11″ treads pass. 15 risers at 7.47″ would pass. Keeping the top landing where it is, the run grows one tread at the bottom: the bottom landing stays 3′-4″ deep and headroom is 6′-11″. Want me to make that change?Yes, fix it.Draft: Creates 1 line on layer Stairs. Reshapes 3 lines. Edits 1 dimension.Open in ScriptsI added the 15th riser, lengthened the guard, handrail, and arrow, and updated the run’s dimension to 12′-10″.Apply this change?Apply EnterDiscard EscOr say what to changeAutoDoes this stair meet code?Checking the stair against the IRCFloor to floor is 9′-4″ (112″) over 14 risers: 8″ each, over the 7¾″ limit. Treads are 11″ (10″ minimum). 112 ÷ 7.75 = 14.45, so 15 risers at 7.47″. With the top landing fixed, the new tread goes at the bottom, so check the bottom landing (36″ minimum) and headroom (6′-8″ minimum).Read the file overviewRead the fileOpen in ScriptsNo. Its 14 risers are 8″ each (9′-4″ floor to floor), and the IRC allows 7¾″. The 11″ treads pass. 15 risers at 7.47″ would pass. Keeping the top landing where it is, the run grows one tread at the bottom: the bottom landing stays 3′-4″ deep and headroom is 6′-11″. Want me to make that change?Yes, fix it.Draft: Creates 1 line on layer Stairs. Reshapes 3 lines. Edits 1 dimension.Open in ScriptsI added the 15th riser, lengthened the guard, handrail, and arrow, and updated the run’s dimension to 12′-10″.Apply this change?Apply EnterDiscard EscOr say what to changeAutoAsked whether a stair meets code, the agent on the command line finds its risers are over the IRC's limit, works out that 15 risers fix it, and, when told to fix it, drafts the change on the plan underneath, waiting for Apply or Discard.Your choice of modelAutoClaudeGPTGeminiDeepSeekGLMand moreHelp with the whole jobIt drafts, models, and writes commands, and renders your model as an image or right in a viewport.Nothing changes without your OKEvery change arrives as a draft, highlighted in the drawing, for you to apply or discard.Right where you workAsk from the command line or the Agents panel, with your choice of model. Threads are saved with the file, private to you.Entirely optionalEverything in Aircad works without it. Use it as much or as little as you like.03/CollaborationAlways up to date. Every change on record.One source of truth for every drawing. No emailed copies, no files checked out, no “final_v3.” Every edit is kept with who made it and when.Sharing and comments in the docsMultiplayer editingShare a link and everyone works in the same file, so there's never a stale copy, and you can see who's working where.Always the latest revisionEveryone edits the same file at once, and each change shows up for everyone as it's made.Comments on the drawingFeedback stays pinned to the spot it's about, not lost in email, so the context is kept as the drawing changes.Review is built inComments, redlines, and marked-up PDFs are part of Aircad. No separate review subscription required.Control who can editShare with a link, and decide who can edit and who can only view.Mounting PlateMCARMMCMaya Chen · 2mCan the bore go to Ø32 for the larger bearing?ARAlex Rivera · nowOpening it up now.Maya ChenAlex Rivera2Two teammates in the same part drawing, each with a named pointer, and a comment thread pinned to the bore asking to enlarge it.A clear record of every change.Every file keeps unlimited version history, so nothing is lost and any change can be traced back.A complete audit trailEvery edit is kept with who made it and when, in an activity feed for the file.Compare any two versionsSee what was added, changed, and deleted, tinted right in the drawing.Fork and editExperiment on a fork from any point in the history. The original stays as it was.Restore earlier workBring back an earlier version whenever you need it. Mounting Plate All changes saved Version historyRev AFromAlex · Yesterday, 16:42Bolt patternYou · Today, 10:18Rev BToAlex · Today, 11:06Current versionYou · Today, 11:32Rev A Rev B5 added2 changed1 removedYour current drawing stays intact while you compare. Restore earlier workA mounting plate compared across two versions in its history: a new bolt pattern tinted as added, a larger bore tinted as changed with its old size ghosted, and a deleted slot ghosted as removed.04/DocumentationDocument everything, beautifully.A drawing set is only as good as its annotation. Dimensions, GD&T, leaders, text, and tables, on layouts with viewports at any scale that print exactly as they look.Annotation in the docsKitchen Faucet - Aircadaircad.com/f/kitchen-faucetEvery dimension typeLinear, angular, radius, diameter, arc length, ordinate, baseline, and continue. Each follows the geometry it measures, so it stays right as the design changes.GD&T and leadersFeature control frames on their own or on a leader, and leaders for notes and callouts.Text, tables, and title blocksStyled text, tables for schedules and parts lists, and title blocks with attributes. Styles keep a whole set consistent.Beautiful view stylesSections with hatching, hidden line from the model, line weights, shadows, and physically based materials, with a print preview that matches the PDF.05/Import & exportBring your files. Take them anywhere.Open DWG and DXF with their layouts, blocks, and dimensions, and bring in Rhino, STEP, glTF, and SVG. Send drawings back as DWG, DXF, or PDF, and models as STL or OBJ.What each format brings in.dwgAutoCAD drawingImport · Export.dxfDrawing exchangeImport · Export.pdfDrawing setExport.3dmRhino modelImport.stepSolid exchangeImport.gltfScene + materialsImport.svgVector artworkImport.stl · .objMeshesImport · ExportPerformanceSerious CAD performance.250,000+ entities in one file. Keep the whole model in one place instead of splitting it across files to keep your CAD responsive.Bundled Tower - Aircadaircad.com/f/bundled-tower108 floors. 38,510 editable solids.Big models stay smoothPan, zoom, and orbit stay fluid with thousands of solids on screen, and repeated parts and blocks barely add to the load.Edits stay quickChanging one part updates just that part, so a big file feels as quick as a small one.Heavy work runs in the backgroundBooleans, edge fillets, lofts, sweeps, and Make2D run off to the side. The drawing stays live, and Esc stops them.Views switch without reloadingSplit the screen, change view styles, or turn on print preview, and the model doesn’t load again.06/ScriptingMake the command you wish you had.Write commands in JavaScript on the same API our built-in commands use: inputs with snaps, live previews, options, and one undo step. Keep them in the file or share them with your team. Or describe the command and let the agent write it.Read the script APIMake a Torus command: pick the center, drag the ring's radius with a preview, then set the tube radius.import { BRep, Curve, Plane } from "aircad";
export const manifest = {
name: "Torus",
kind: "command",
capabilities: ["document:read", "document:write"],
inputs: {
center: { type: "point", prompt: "Pick the center" },
radius: { type: "length", prompt: "Major radius" },
tube: { type: "length", prompt: "Tube radius" },
},
api: 1,
};
export default async function main(cad) {
const center = await cad.input.point("center");
// Draw the ring while the pointer moves.
const ring = cad.display.show();
const radius = await cad.input.length("radius", {
from: center,
onChange: (r) => ring.set(Curve.circle(Plane.at(center), r)),
});
const tube = await cad.input.length("tube");
return cad.doc.add(BRep.torus(Plane.at(center), radius, tube));
}import { BRep, Curve, Plane } from "aircad";
